      "content": "Don't worry, it's probably just a minor case of heat rash, but I'll give you some extra insurance. The spots you're describing, especially if they're purple, are more likely to be a viral rash, like roseola. I'm not saying it's a serious condition, but you should still get your child some rest, and I recommend a dose of acetaminophen to bring down the fever. And, just to be on the safe side, give your little one a shot of ibuprofen to reduce the inflammation.",
