      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For acetaminophen, give your child 5-10 mg/kg every 4-6 hours, so for a 4-year-old, that's about 1-2 teaspoons. And for ibuprofen, start with 1-2 mg/kg every 6 hours, so for a 4-year-old, that's about 1/4 to 1/2 teaspoon. As for lethargy, it's normal for kids to be tired when they're sick, but if he's not responding to fluids and rest, it's a good sign to keep an eye on him. I'd recommend a dose of vitamin C to boost his immune system, and maybe some chicken soup to soothe his throat.",
